237: differ in the way they treat values whose least significant digit is 5.
238-The 
239-convergent
240- function rounds ties to the nearest even integer.
241-The 
242-nearest
243- function rounds ties to the nearest integer toward positive infinity.
244-The 
245-round
246- function rounds ties to the nearest integer with greater absolute value.
247-This example illustrates these differences for a given input, a.
248-a = fi([-3.5:3.5]&#39;);
